{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["To know the truth, if your heart desires, see all her host honored in her dwelling, and the Urim and Thummim and their secret I will reveal in hiddenness, in order, ואתה תצוה." "<b>ואתה תצוה.</b> I will first mention the reason for joining the pericope, for when he finished recording all the sacred vessels, and the curtain and the tabernacle and the tent and the covering and the altar of burnt offering and the court and the screen, he began to explain the service of the tabernacle, and what their service is in itself — no outsider among them — and he began that they kindle lamps with olive oil, not with strange oil. And these servants are fit to be distinguished and set apart by their families and by their garments, and Scripture mentioned these one after the other. And afterward Scripture mentioned that they are obligated to be trained during the seven days of ordination, that Moses train them and accustom them, and afterward they serve and offer the daily burnt offering on the altar of burnt offering, not on the golden altar — only that they burn incense upon it and make atonement on its horns once a year." "<b>And the sense of ואתה תצוה.</b> That it is an eternal commandment upon the public to supply olive oil continually to kindle the regular lamp. And do not wonder concerning the oil that the princes brought, for that was anointing oil; rather, oil for the luminary is an obligation of the public. And there is a custom in places where olives grow, that they select the pure olive — the meaning is berries that have no blemish, or that some of them have not been eaten — and from it they make oil for the food of kings; therefore Scripture mentioned זך (pure) before כתית (beaten):" "<b>למאור (for the luminary).</b> For the need of light at night." "<b>להעלות (to cause to ascend).</b> To kindle the lamps. And concerning the lampstand of Solomon it is written לבערם כמשפט (2 Chronicles 4:20):" "<b>And the sense of תמיד (regular/continual).</b> Every single night. And there is a use of the word תמיד more difficult than this: והיה על מצחו תמיד (Exodus 28:38) — whenever the turban is placed on his head, they must always place the holy diadem upon it:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "This acrostic/poetic passage is textually obscure; translated hyper-literally. The opening letters of the first six words spell לאברהם (to Abraham). The reference to Urim, Thummim, and sod hints at a hidden reading of ואתה תצוה (Exodus 27:20); the acrostic letters of the verse permuting to spell the divine name. Translated without explanation per discipline."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:54.923729116Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}